{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>The days of</b> — Perhaps a disputant will dispute: Was not Moses 120 years old, and how can he say \"seventy years\"? This is a sign that the poet's name was Moses, and the answer is thus: we can say that Noah, Daniel, and Job are not well known — but behold, at the beginning he is called \"the man of Elohim,\" and on this account he mentioned that he does not involve himself with the vanities of the world. And thus the meaning of this psalm: Moses speaks in the language of every generation, and his generation too was thus until today. Perhaps he made this prayer before he prophesied, when he was eighty years old and his hands were heavy." "<b>And if in them</b> — it would be a great thing if they were in number seventy years." "<b>And their pride</b> — And the days of their pride are the days of might and strength, which are the days of youth; all of them are toil and trouble." "<b>For it is cut off</b> — that they are cut off quickly, like \"cut off your tassel\" (גזי נזרך), and this is the meaning of חיש ונעופה — and behold, we become like a wandering bird from its place. Or ונעופה — to dwell in a land of darkness, a land of gloom; \"making dawn dark\" — עושה שחר עיפה. Or the word is from the root עפעף, like \"they fly away like the morning\" (תעופה כבוקר), \"you weary your eyes upon him and he is not\" (תהיה התעיף עיניך בו ואיננו), and as though תעופה were our days."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 90, :notes {0 "Reading והלא יראה as 'but behold, he is called,' resolving an ambiguous clause; the phrase 'his hands were heavy' may allude to Exodus 17:12 but the reference is uncertain in context."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:54.387927178Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}